= Homeostasis =
Homeostasis is the maintenance of internal conditions within ranges compatible with continued system function despite external or internal disturbance.

== Biological systems ==
In organisms, homeostasis includes regulation of variables such as temperature, pH, glucose, osmotic balance, gases, and ion concentrations through coordinated sensing and response.

== Systems perspective ==
Homeostasis is not static equilibrium. It is dynamic regulation: continuous adjustment through feedback, buffering, redundancy, and control processes.

